Activity 1: Computational Thinking Exercise (Started during ILP and finished during the next F2F)

Instructions:
Choose between the worksheets “Smart School Canteen Queue” or “Smart Vending Machine” in Annex A or Annex B.
Make a copy of the chosen Annex as your first graded exercise in your Github Portfolio under quarter1 or q1 folder and name it as ctskillsSectionLN.md.  
Read the simple scenario provided in the worksheet and your task is to decompose the problem into smaller manageable parts that could be answered or solved with computational thinking skills.
Follow the steps in the worksheet. Work on this during one of your ILPs this week but before our next F2F meeting. Please be prepared to be called for your short presentation of your answers.
Select one of your identified sub-problems and design an algorithmic solution using a flowchart or pseudocode.
Refer to the rubrics for grading in Annex A or Annex B.
Update also your README.md file to have the link to your file and submit the live server link  and the .git repository link in your official Learning Management System (i.e. KHub or Google Classroom).
This is graded and will be recorded under the formative assessment..
